WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:07.490
Groups let you update related devices together. We’ll choose a
release, send it to a group, and check the device’s result.

2
00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:13.509
In Devices, open Device groups. Create a group for the devices
you want to manage together.

3
00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:19.274
Use Manage to add devices. This example reuses a group that is
already available.

4
00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:23.922
In the library, choose Deploy this version for the release you
want to send.

5
00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:28.925
Select the group. Desired state keeps this version requested for
its members.

6
00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:34.351
Review and approve the deployment. Device clients will process
it when they are ready.

7
00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:42.543
The deployment is created. That confirms your request, rather
than a completed installation.

8
00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:49.039
Open Deployments after the client has processed the update.
Check the result reported by the device.

9
00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:56.839
Applied means the device completed its configured installer. It
does not establish that a long-running service is healthy.

10
00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:04.426
Applied confirms the device completed its installer. Check
device health separately before expanding your deployment.
